The isometry used subsequently is $cal(U)_(q \, d) = iota_(q \, d)
  U_(q \, d) \( 1 \)$ restricted to $Z_(n \, q - d)$. By Equation (4.2),
  its image is exactly the subspace with $d$ south-pole zeros.

